{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → ~48.5% acc), we have zero evidence about whether the image modality carries any independent predictive signal. This is the single most important uncertainty to resolve before investing in any multimodal or fusion configurations. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the simplest, cleanest image-only baseline: it changes exactly one high-level dimension (modality) relative to config_001 while keeping profile setting, aggregation, and fusion at their minimal defaults. If image alone approaches or exceeds the RNA baseline, it confirms the image modality is informative and justifies pursuing multimodal fusion (configs 016–051). If image alone is substantially worse, it tells us to focus the remaining budget on improving the RNA side (learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation) rather than spending experiments on multimodal configurations that may not benefit from a weak second modality. This experiment maximizes information gain per trial under a limited budget by resolving a binary, strategy-shaping question that no other single experiment can answer."
}

